Royal jelly isn't honey, though. Honey is partially digested nectar
that bees use as an easy-to-store food source. Royal jelly is (and I'm
admittedly trusting Wikipedia on this one) a secretion of their
hypopharyngeal glands, and is a vital agent in the development of
larva. It's very perishable, and for human purposes is usually mixed
with honey for storage, but I doubt that the royal jelly one finds in
NetHack has been thus mixed.

Except that I don't think royal jelly rots at the moment. Either
that's an oversight, or it is indeed mixed with honey and this is a
decent idea. However, adding to max hp doesn't make much sense... that
would allow an uninjured first-level tourist to nearly double his HP.
when he was obviously not injured in the first place and not in need
of antiseptic. Maybe heal a few hp's, but then the obvious choice is
to eat it...


